  <title>Lesson Activities</title>
  <para>Here are the instructional activities for the lesson:</para>
  <list>
    <item>2.6.1: Multiplying Equations by a Number </item>
    <item>2.6.2: Writing a New System to Solve a Given System <list>
        <item>2.6.2: Self Check </item>
        <item>2.6.2: Additional Resources</item>
      </list>
    </item>
    <item>2.6.3: Finding Solutions to Unordered Sets of Equivalent Systems  <list>
        <item>2.6.3: Self Check </item>
        <item>2.6.3: Additional Resources</item>
      </list>
    </item>
    <item>2.6.4: Building Equivalent Systems </item>
  </list>
</div>
<div><span>Students will also complete a series of problems in the 2.6.5: Practice.</span></div>
<div>
  <title>Required Materials</title>
  <list>
    <item>Graphing technology</item>
    <item>Pre-printed slips, cut from copies of the <link url="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/44bc8768abb54e8e3ed6544ec6108f910b72028d">blackline master</link></item>
  </list>
  <title>Required Preparation</title>
  <para>Acquire devices that can run Desmos (recommended) or other graphing technology. It is ideal if each student has their own device.Be prepared to display a graph using technology for all to see.</para>
